# CtrlIRL-Coder pipeline template — multi-layer compositor (MPEG-TS).
#
# Layers (see scene.example.json) feed the `compositor` element; this template
# has no upstream source of its own. The composited frames are encoded + audio-
# muxed to MPEG-TS and end in the same terminal sink as example-full.pipeline:
# `appsink name=appsink`, which ctrlirl-coder pulls (gst_app_sink_pull_sample)
# and sends over SRT (destination from config.toml [srt] uri). The appsink is
# also the stats surface for the adaptive bitrate controller (frame liveness,
# encoded throughput, caps framerate).
#
# Contract elements:
#   compositor — multi-layer scene (layers attached via sink_%d pads)
#   appsink    — terminal sink (MANDATORY; Go pulls + sends SRT)
#   venc_kbps  — x264enc encoder (bitrate property in kbit/s)
#   mux        — mpegtsmux (browser layers attach their page audio here)

# Audio is not a static test tone: every audio-producing layer feeds a
# raw-PCM chain into one shared `audiomixer → voaacenc → aacparse` tail on
# a single pad of the `mux` element below — one audio program total,
# because MPEG-TS demuxers (OBS) only play the stream's first program.
# Browser layers capture the page's audio on their Pulse/PipeWire null-sink
# monitors (`pulsesrc → audioconvert → <audio filters>`); video layers feed
# their source's audio track (SRT / HTTP / file: decodebin audio pad →
# audioconvert → queue). A scene with no such layers streams video-only.

# IMPORTANT: the caps after the compositor MUST pin format + width + height +
# framerate to the scene size. The compositor (GStreamer 1.28) resolves its
# output caps from upstream video info at negotiate time; with a live appsrc
# frontend that info is not ready during preroll, so a bare `format=I420`
# (or any non-pinning caps) makes the compositor lock to its 1x1 default and
# the encoder never receives a frame. Keep width/height/framerate in sync with
# the scene definition (scene.example.json: 1280x720 @ 30fps). A scene larger
# than the pin gets squashed into it — use example-layered-1080p60.pipeline
# for 1920x1080 @ 60fps scenes.
compositor name=compositor background=black
  ! videoconvert
  ! video/x-raw,format=I420,width=1280,height=720,framerate=30/1
  ! x264enc speed-preset=superfast tune=zerolatency bitrate=6000 key-int-max=30 name=venc_kbps
  ! h264parse config-interval=1
  ! mux.
mpegtsmux name=mux
  ! appsink name=appsink

# Scene: see scene.example.json. Attach with:
#   ctrlirl-coder --config config.toml --pipeline pipeline/example-layered.pipeline --scene scene.example.json
